.TH PRINTF 3 "27 Jan 2026" "1.0" "Holberton School C Library"
.SH NAME
printf \- prints formatted output to stdout
.SH SYNOPSIS
#include <stdio.h>

int printf(const char *format, ...);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBprintf\fR function sends formatted output to \fBstdout\fR.  
The function supports conversion specifiers for integers, characters, strings, and more.  
The number and type of arguments must correspond to the format string.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Upon successful return, \fBprintf\fR returns the number of characters printed (excluding the null byte used to end output to strings).  
If an output error is encountered, a negative value is returned.
.SH EXAMPLE
printf("Hello, %s!\n", "world"); 
.SH SEE ALSO
fprintf(3), sprintf(3), snprintf(3)
